questions.explanation:
According to the text, Henry Moseley observed 'A plot of $\sqrt{
u}$ (where $
u$ is frequency of X-rays emitted) against atomic number (Z) gave a straight line and not the plot of $\sqrt{
u}$ vs atomic mass.' This observation established atomic number as a more fundamental property. Option A describes the plot that did not yield a straight line. Options C and D are not the variables Moseley used for his linear plot.
